# Backend Patterns

## Module layout
`*.module.ts` → `*.controller.ts` (thin) → `*.service.ts` (logic) → `ports/*.port.ts` → `adapters/prisma-*.repository.ts`

## Controller
- Validate with DTO + Zod/class-validator
- Delegate to service immediately — no Prisma in controller

## Service
- Inject repository **port** via DI token — not PrismaService directly
- Business logic only — no HTTP, no env vars, no SDK imports

## Repository adapter
- Implements port interface; Prisma/SQL lives here only
- Tenant scope on every query (`compCode` from method args, not global state alone)

## Service transaction pattern
```typescript
await this.dcrRepo.submit(compCode, input, async (tx) => {
  // adapter runs prisma.$transaction internally OR accepts tx client
});
```

## Tenant context
Always pass `compCode` from authenticated context into service methods — never from request body alone.

## API response
Return `{ responseCode, errorObj, data }` — business errors use `417`.

## Tests
- `*.service.spec.ts` — mock repository port
- E2E — real adapters against test DB
